%T A039821 68858583810,28797022447980,58526378304180,34009655736503400,
%U A039821 68787420596367165,52951950764170220070,106784276647367492470,105101499476653341847900,211545958093387212124726
%N A039821 Numerators in Stirling expansion of central binomial coefficient C(2*n,n).
%C A039821 a(j) is exactly divisible by 2^([ binary digit sum of j ]-1) (see reference).
%C A039821 From _Natalia L. Skirrow_, Aug 04 2026: (Start)
%C A039821 This is not the most efficient series to use! The one in terms of n-1/4 (with coefficients from A006934/A123854) is an even function so requires half as many terms be evaluated for the same precision; see Luschny, Elezović, StackExchange links.
%C A039821 A result of Frenzen (1987) states that this series is enveloping; the error from truncating the series is always the same sign as (and bounded by) the first omitted term. (End)
%D A039821 D. B. Tyler, D. Hickerson, unpublished correspondence, 1985-8; cf. below reference.
%H A039821 Natalia L. Skirrow, <a href="/A039821/b039821.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..256</a>
%H A039821 Neven Elezović, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL17/Elezovic/elezovic5.html">Asymptotic Expansions of Central Binomial Coefficients and Catalan Numbers</a>. Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 17 (2014), article 14.2.1.
%H A039821 C. L. Frenzen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1137/0518067">Error Bounds for Asymptotic Expansions of the Ratio of Two Gamma Functions</a>. SIAM Journal on Mathematical Analysis, vol. 18, iss. 3 (1987).
%H A039821 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://www.luschny.de/math/factorial/approx/SimpleCases.html">Approximation Formulas for the Factorial Function</a>.
%H A039821 R. Richberg, D. E. Knuth (independently), <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324649">Problem 6581: The asymptotic expansion of the Middle Binomial Coefficient</a>, Amer. Math. Monthly, 97 (7) 1990, 626-630.
%H A039821 Natalia L. Skirrow, <a href="https://oeis.org/wiki/User:Natalia_L._Skirrow/Stirling&#39;s_approximations">Stirling's approximations</a>.
%H A039821 Natalia L. Skirrow, <a href="https://math.stackexchange.com/a/5144931">answer to "Elementary central binomial coefficient estimates"</a> (2026), Mathematics StackExchange.
%F A039821 From _Natalia L. Skirrow_, Aug 03 2026: (Start)
%F A039821 Let coeff(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} (-1)^k*C(2n, n)*C(2n, n-k)*Stirling2(n+k, k)*(2n+1)/(2k+1).
%F A039821 a(n) = |coeff(n)|/2 = -(-1)^floor(n/2) * coeff(n)/2.
%F A039821 Let f(x) = sqrt(x)*Gamma(x+1/2)/Gamma(x+1) = binomial(2*x, x)*sqrt(Pi*x)/4^x.
%F A039821 f(x) = sqrt(x/Pi) * Integral_{t=0..oo} e^(-(x+1/4)*t) / sqrt(2*sinh(t/2)) dt (a Laplace transform).
%F A039821 The following asymptotic expansions hold as formal power series:
%F A039821 log(f(x)) ~ Sum_{k>=1} Bernoulli(2k)*(1/4^k - 1)/(k*(2k-1)*x^(2k-1)).
%F A039821 f(x) ~ Sum_{n>=0} coeff(n)/(16*x)^n = 1 - 2*Sum_{n>=1} a(n)*(-1)^floor(n/2)/(16*x)^n.
%F A039821 coeff(n)/16^n is the extension of the degree-2n polynomial |Stirling1(x, x-n)| to x=1/2.
%F A039821 E.g.f. of coeff(n)/C(2*n, n): sqrt( 2*x/sinh(2*x) ) * e^(-x).
%F A039821 coeff(n) = C(2*n, n) * B^(1/2)_n(1/2) * (-4)^n, where B^(r)_n(x) is a Nørlund polynomial.
%F A039821 coeff(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} (-1)^k * A068555(n+k, k) * A008299(n+k, k) * 4^(n-k).
%F A039821 coeff(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} (-1)^k * A068555(2*n, k) * A008517(n, k), with the extension A008517(n, 0) = [n=0].
%F A039821 Recurrence: coeff(n) = Sum_{k=1..n, k odd} coeff(n-k) * Bernoulli(k+1) * 8^k * (1-2^(k+1)) / (k+1).
%F A039821 |coeff(n)| ~ n!*C(2n, n)^2*(2 if n odd, Pi/2n if n even)/(2*Pi)^n.
%F A039821 |coeff(n)/16^n| ~ n!*(2 if n odd, Pi/2n if n even)/(Pi*n*(2*Pi)^n).
%F A039821 Logarithmically differentiating the asymptotic shows that when using this series to approximate binomial(2*x, x), it reaches maximal precision approximately at 2*Pi*x summands before beginning to diverge.
%F A039821 coeff(n)/16^n = A143503(n)/A088802(n). (End)
%e A039821 C(2*n,n) ~ (4^n/sqrt(Pi*n)) * (1 - 2/m + 2/m^2 + 20/m^3 - 42/m^4 - ...), where m = 16*n.
%e A039821 sqrt(2*t/sinh(2*t)) * e^-t = 1 - 2*t/(1!*C(2,1)) + 2*t^2/(2!*C(4,2)) + 20*t^3/(3!*C(6,3)) - 42*t^4/(4!*C(8,4)) - ...
%t A039821 r:=Range[0,20]
%t A039821 Abs[FullSimplify[CoefficientList[Series[Sqrt[2*t/Sinh[2*t]]*E^-t,{t,0,20}],t]*Binomial[2*r,r]*r!]][[2;;]]/2 (* _Natalia L. Skirrow_, Aug 03 2026 *)
%o A039821 (Python)
%o A039821 from sympy import bernoulli
%o A039821 from functools import cache
%o A039821 stirlog=cache(lambda k: k and int(bernoulli(k+1) * 8**k * (1-2*2**k)) //(k+1))
%o A039821 # stirlog(2*k) = 0, stirlog(2*k-1) = (-1)^k*A253165(k-1) * 2^(2*k-1) = (-1)^k*A002105(k) * 2^(5*k-4)
%o A039821 coeff=cache(lambda n: not n or sum(stirlog(k) * coeff(n-k) for k in range(1, n+1, 2))//n)
%o A039821 A039821=lambda n: abs(coeff(n))>>1
%o A039821 print([A039821(n) for n in range(20)]) # _Natalia L. Skirrow_, Aug 11 2026
%o A039821 (SageMath)
%o A039821 def A039821_list(N):
%o A039821     R.<x> = PowerSeriesRing(QQ, default_prec=N + 2)
%o A039821     coeffs = [QQ(0)] * (N + 2); coeffs[0] = QQ(1)
%o A039821     if N >= 1: coeffs[1] = QQ(-2)
%o A039821     fact = 2; pow4 = 16
%o A039821     for n in range(2, N + 2):
%o A039821         if n % 2 == 0: coeffs[n] = QQ(bernoulli(n) * pow4) / fact
%o A039821         fact *= (n + 1); pow4 *= 4
%o A039821     f = R(coeffs).sqrt()
%o A039821     ans = []; scale = 1
%o A039821     for n in range(1, N + 1):
%o A039821         scale *= (4 * n - 2)
%o A039821         a = ZZ(f[n] * scale)
%o A039821         ans.append(abs(a) // 2)
%o A039821     return ans
%o A039821 A039821_list(20)  # _Peter Luschny_, Aug 11 2026
%Y A039821 Cf. A143503/A088802 (this series in reduced fraction form).
%Y A039821 Cf. A000984 (central binomial coefficients), A008299 (second-order Stirling subset numbers), A008517 (second-order Eulerian numbers), A027641/A027642 (Bernoulli numbers), A068555, A253165.
